arXiv:2510.08102v1 [cs.CL] 09 Oct 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Lossless Vocabulary Reduction 
<br class="ltx_break">for Auto-Regressive Language Models</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">
<span id="id1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="id1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="id1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Daiki Chijiwa<sup id="id1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>  , Taku Hasegawa<sup id="id1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>, Kyosuke Nishida<sup id="id1.1.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>, Shin’ya Yamaguchi<sup id="id1.1.1.4" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>,</span></span>
<span id="id1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="id1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Tomoya Ohba<sup id="id1.2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>,
Tamao Sakao<sup id="id1.2.1.2" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>, Susumu Takeuchi<sup id="id1.2.1.3" class="ltx_sup">1</sup></span></span>
</span>
</span>


<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="id2" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>NTT Computer and Data Science Laboratories, NTT Corporation 
<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="id3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>NTT Human Informatics Laboratories, NTT Corporation
</span><span id="id4" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_correspondence ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>Correspondence to: <span id="id4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">daiki.chijiwa@ntt.com</span></span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Tokenization—the process of decomposing a given text into a sequence of subwords called <span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tokens</span>—is one of the key components in the development of language models.
Particularly, auto-regressive language models generate texts token by token, i.e., by predicting the next-token distribution given the previous ones, and thus tokenization directly affects their efficiency in text generation.
Since each language model has their own vocabulary as a set of possible tokens, they struggle to cooperate with each other at the level of next-token distributions such as model ensemble.
In this paper, we establish a theoretical framework of lossless vocabulary reduction, which efficiently converts a given auto-regressive language model into the one with an arbitrarily small vocabulary without any loss in accuracy.
As an application, we demonstrate that language models with different tokenization can cooperate with each other efficiently through their maximal common vocabulary.</p>
  
</div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="p1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:24.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tokenization—the process of decomposing a given text into a sequence of subwords called <span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tokens</span>—plays an important role in modern language models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schuster &amp; Nakajima, 2012</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sennrich et al., 2016</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kudo, 2018</a>)</cite>, where tokens are the minimum unit for their input and output.
Particularly, tokenization largely affects the efficiency of text generation with auto-regressive language models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2019</a>)</cite> which are trained to generate texts by first computing the next-token distribution given previous tokens and then sampling a token from it iteratively.
In other words, the longer tokens are sampled at each iteration on average, the less number of sampling iterations is required for text generation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each language model has its own <span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">vocabulary</span>, the set of all possible tokens, which is generally constructed based on the statistics in their training data so that more plausible texts can be represented by less numbers of tokens.
As a result, given two (or more) language models that have been trained independently with distinct training data, their vocabularies do not match in general.
Due to the vocabulary mismatch, <span id="S1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">language models with different tokenizers or vocabularies struggle to cooperate with each other at the level of their next-token distributions</span>, such as ensemble <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hinton, 1999</a>)</cite>, knowledge distillation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hinton et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, speculative decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leviathan et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, inference-time alignment <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mitchell et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, etc.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To this problem, recent work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vieira et al., 2025</a>)</cite> have proposed a theoretically-guaranteed approach that reduces a given next-token distribution to the corresponding next-<span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">byte</span> distribution, without changing the distribution of generated texts.
In other words, the resulting byte-level distribution is equivalent to the original token-level one as a probabilistic text generator, while its vocabulary being restricted to the set of all one-byte tokens, <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathtt{0x00}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟶</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟶𝟶</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathtt{0x00}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathtt{0xFF}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟶</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙵</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathtt{0xFF}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
This approach enables language models with different vocabularies to cooperate with each other, at the level of their next-byte distributions.
However, the byte-level cooperation leads to increased inference costs by its nature, since each model has to predict byte by byte instead of tokens with multiple bytes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, beyond the byte-level reduction, we establish the first theoretical framework called <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lossless vocabulary reduction</span> that reduces a given next-token distribution to the corresponding one over an <span id="S1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">arbitrary sub-vocabulary</span> without changing its behavior as a text generator (<a href="#S2.F1" title="In 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), which is achieved by introducing the new notion of <span id="S1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nested tokenization</span>.
Then we derive an efficient approximated algorithm to compute it with negligibly small overhead.
As an application, we propose to cooperate language models with different vocabularies by lossless reduction to their <span id="S1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">maximal common vocabulary</span> among them.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, our contributions in this paper can be summarized as follows:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We established the first theoretical framework of lossless vocabulary reduction and derived an efficient approximated algorithm that converts given next-token distributions over some vocabulary to the equivalent distributions over its arbitrary sub-vocabulary in inference-time. We also provided an illustrative example of how it actually works following our theory.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experimental results with several language models show that the derived algorithm is actually almost lossless as our theory suggests. Also, experimental results on ensemble show that ensemble over the maximal common vocabulary achieves comparable accuracy to the byte-level ensemble while the former is more efficient than the latter.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08102v1/20250922_Figure_1.svg" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:519/134;" width="519" height="134"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Overview of lossless vocabulary reduction. Instead of sampling tokens from the original next-token distribution over <math id="S2.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can inductively compute and sample from the equivalent distribution over the sub-vocabulary <math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> while keeping its accuracy. See <a href="#S3" title="3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for notations and details.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, we assume that any text is a sequence of bytes obtained by some character encoding, typically by UTF-8 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yergeau, 2003</a>)</cite>.
In this section, we briefly introduce the formal definitions and properties of texts, tokenization, and language models.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Formulation of Tokens</h3>

<section id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Texts.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of symbols, such as all alphabets or all characters.
Throughout this paper, <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is considered as a set of all bytes, i.e., <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-bit strings <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{1}\cdots b_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>8</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\cdots b_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{*}:=\bigcup_{k=1}^{\infty}A^{k}\cup\{\emptyset\}=\{a_{1}\cdots a_{N}\mid a_{i}\in\mathcal{A},N\in\mathbb{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{*}:=\bigcup_{k=1}^{\infty}A^{k}\cup\{\emptyset\}=\{a_{1}\cdots a_{N}\mid a_{i}\in\mathcal{A},N\in\mathbb{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              The construction of <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is also known as the Kleene closure of <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="footnote1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> means the empty string.</span></span></span> be the set of all finite sequences of bytes with an empty symbol <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
We often use the notation <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}:=a_{1}\cdots a_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}:=a_{1}\cdots a_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.
Here we briefly note that (1) <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of only <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> elements, obviously less than all symbols in the real world, (2) <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of all possible texts in computers because they are represented by sequences of bytes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tokenization.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A tokenization scheme <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is formally defined<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              Throughout this paper, we focus only on deterministic tokenization which is widely employed in modern language models.</span></span></span> as a triplet <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{V},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{V},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>, with a finite set of vocabulary <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, an encoder <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}:\mathcal{A}^{*}\to\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}:\mathcal{A}^{*}\to\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and a decoder <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}}:\mathcal{V}^{*}\to\mathcal{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}}:\mathcal{V}^{*}\to\mathcal{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}]_{\mathcal{A}}=a_{1:N}\text{ for all texts }a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*},\text{and }" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> for all texts </mtext><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext>and </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}]_{\mathcal{A}}=a_{1:N}\text{ for all texts }a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*},\text{and }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}=[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{A}}\cdots[x_{T}]_{\mathcal{A}}\text{ for all tokens }x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mtext> for all tokens </mtext><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}=[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{A}}\cdots[x_{T}]_{\mathcal{A}}\text{ for all tokens }x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is called a token in <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and has its textual representation <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x]_{\mathcal{A}}\in\mathcal{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x]_{\mathcal{A}}\in\mathcal{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> given by the decoder.
The encoder <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> uniquely converts a given text <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to the corresponding tokens <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> with some length <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that the condition (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Tokenization. ‣ 2.1 Formulation of Tokens ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) has first appeared in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kudo &amp; Richardson (2018)</a></cite> by treating texts as a sequence of Unicode bytes such as UTF-8 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yergeau, 2003</a>)</cite>, which is now employed by most of modern language models after <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al. (2019)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Formulation and Properties of Language Models</h3>

<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Language model over tokens.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math> be the true distribution of natural language texts, defined over sequences of <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-bit binaries <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A language model <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math>, with respect to the tokenization <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}=(\mathcal{V},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}=(\mathcal{V},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined as the probabilistic distribution over sequences of tokens <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that matches the distribution of the encoded sequences <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> of natural texts <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}\sim p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}\sim p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>.
In other words, it is defined as</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T}):=\begin{cases}p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N}),&amp;\text{if }x_{1:T}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}\text{ for some (unique) }a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>text</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mtext> for some (unique) </mtext><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T}):=\begin{cases}p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N}),&amp;\text{if }x_{1:T}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}\text{ for some (unique) }a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then we say that <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> is a token distribution associated with the true text distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Next-token distribution.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From a computational perspective, it is infeasible to implement the token distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> directly. Rather, it is standard to implement its <span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">next-token distribution</span> denoted as <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we formally define here.
First of all, let us introduce <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}*</annotation></semantics></math> in shorthand, a set of all tokens starting with <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1}\cdots x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\cdots x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*:=\{x_{1}\cdots x_{t}x_{t+1}\cdots x_{T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}\mid x_{t+1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},T\in\mathbb{N}\}\subset\mathcal{V}^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*:=\{x_{1}\cdots x_{t}x_{t+1}\cdots x_{T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}\mid x_{t+1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},T\in\mathbb{N}\}\subset\mathcal{V}^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which plays a central role here. We can consider the corresponding probability to this event:</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*)=\sum_{x_{1:T}\in x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\cdots x_{t}x_{t+1}\cdots x_{T})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*)=\sum_{x_{1:T}\in x_{1}\cdots x_{t}*}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\cdots x_{t}x_{t+1}\cdots x_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Now the next-token distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the conditional probability</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1}):=p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*\mid x_{1:t-1}*)=\frac{p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)}{p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t-1}*)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1}):=p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*\mid x_{1:t-1}*)=\frac{p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)}{p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t-1}*)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We can sample a full sequence <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from the distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> by recursively sampling <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from the next-token distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> starting from the empty string <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, it is sufficient to implement the next-token distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> for the task of sequential text generation from <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Throughout this paper, we assume that the next-token distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t}\mid x_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed for all <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> in parallel by a single unit of computation, as an output of a neural network followed by the softmax layer over the vocabulary <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Valid tokens and minimal covering.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of tokens.
We call <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <em id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">valid tokens</em> if it satisfies the following inverse relation of <a href="#S2.E1" title="In Tokenization. ‣ 2.1 Formulation of Tokens ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=x_{1:T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=x_{1:T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In other words, <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> is valid if and only if it can be obtained by tokenizing some text <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Indeed, in the latter case, we can see <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> is valid since <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=[[[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}=x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=[[[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}=x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#S2.E1" title="In Tokenization. ‣ 2.1 Formulation of Tokens ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Obviously, if <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid tokens, it is obtained by tokenizing <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}:=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}:=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the stringification of <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math>, clearly followed by <a href="#S2.E6" title="In Valid tokens and minimal covering. ‣ 2.2 Formulation and Properties of Language Models ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
Note that <a href="#S2.E6" title="In Valid tokens and minimal covering. ‣ 2.2 Formulation and Properties of Language Models ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> generally does not hold solely by <a href="#S2.E1" title="In Tokenization. ‣ 2.1 Formulation of Tokens ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and actually most sequences of tokens are invalid <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is easy to see that the language model <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> associated with the true text distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following <em id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">validity condition</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al., 2024</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})=0,\ \ \ \text{ for any invalid tokens }x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.667em">,</mo><mtext> for any invalid tokens </mtext><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})=0,\ \ \ \text{ for any invalid tokens }x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, by the above discussion, the invalid tokens <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> is never obtained by tokenizing any text <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the definition of <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> falls into the second case in <a href="#S2.E2" title="In Language model over tokens. ‣ 2.2 Formulation and Properties of Language Models ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Importantly, the validity condition leads to simplification of probability computation for language models.
To explain it, let us define the minimal cover <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math> for given texts <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:N}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N}):=\{x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}\mid a_{1:N}\not\prec[x_{1:T-1}]_{\mathcal{A}},a_{1:N}\prec[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}},\text{and }x_{1:T}\text{ is valid.}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊀</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>and </mtext><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> is valid.</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N}):=\{x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}\mid a_{1:N}\not\prec[x_{1:T-1}]_{\mathcal{A}},a_{1:N}\prec[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}},\text{and }x_{1:T}\text{ is valid.}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Note that this is not an empty set because <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}\in C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}\in C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math> always holds.
Using this notion, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al. (2025)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vieira et al. (2025)</a></cite> provided the following formula for computing the underlying distribution over alphabets from the language model over tokens:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vieira et al. (2025)</a></cite>)<span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> be any vocabulary and <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the token distribution associated with the text distribution <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any string <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1}\cdots a_{N}\in\mathcal{A}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\cdots a_{N}\in\mathcal{A}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1}\cdots a_{N}*)=\sum_{x_{1:T}\in C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\cdots x_{T}*)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1}\cdots a_{N}*)=\sum_{x_{1:T}\in C_{\mathcal{V}}(a_{1:N})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\cdots x_{T}*).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since the minimal cover contains only valid tokens, the sum of the right-hand side will be computationally feasible, contrary to the case without the validity condition where the minimal cover may grow exponentially.
In particular, based on this formula, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al. (2025)</a></cite> derived an efficient algorithm to compute the next-byte distribution <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{t}\mid a_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{t}\mid a_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> from the one over tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Lossless Vocabulary Reduction</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we establish a theory and derive an algorithm to restrict the token vocabulary <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> of a language model <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> to any given sub-vocabulary <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, without changing its behavior as a text generator.
The theory and algorithm in this section will be leveraged for cooperation of language models with different vocabularies in the later sections.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Formulation of Vocabulary Reduction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that we have a language model <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math>, a distribution over tokens in a vocabulary <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with the true text distribution <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote its tokenizer <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}}=(\mathcal{V},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}}=(\mathcal{V},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Nested tokenization.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\subset\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\subset\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sub-vocabulary, i.e., an arbitrary subset of the given vocabulary <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> be some tokenization scheme with the sub-vocabulary.
Here we do not necessarily impose any relation between <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> except for the inclusion between the vocabularies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given such a tokenization scheme <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with the sub-vocabulary <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define the <em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">nested tokenization</em> <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}},[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> that tokenizes text by applying <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:=[[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\text{ for }a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*},\text{ with }" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mtext> for </mtext><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> with </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:=[[a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\text{ for }a_{1:N}\in\mathcal{A}^{*},\text{ with }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:=[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}},\ [x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:=[[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\text{ for }x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><mtext> for </mtext><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:=[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}},\ [x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:=[[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\text{ for }x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we abuse the notation <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for denoting both <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:\mathcal{A}^{*}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:\mathcal{A}^{*}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:\mathcal{V}^{*}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}:\mathcal{V}^{*}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{-}]_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for simplicity.
The nested tokenization will play a central role in our vocabulary reduction.
If we consider the case of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}=\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}=\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{A}}=(\mathcal{A},\mathrm{id}_{\mathcal{A}},\mathrm{id}_{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{A}}=(\mathcal{A},\mathrm{id}_{\mathcal{A}},\mathrm{id}_{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the nested tokenization <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is just the stringification of given tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Vocabulary reduction.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we introduce a new language model <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})</annotation></semantics></math> over tokens in the sub-vocabulary <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is induced by the given language model <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> and the nested tokenization <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})}[\mathds{1}\{y_{1:K}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\}]=\mathbb{P}(y_{1:K}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})}[\mathds{1}\{y_{1:K}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\}]=\mathbb{P}(y_{1:K}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">i.e., the probability that <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:K}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained as a re-tokenization of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by the sub-vocabulary <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We call <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})</annotation></semantics></math> the <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">vocabulary reduction</span> of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For example, if we employ the above <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the nested tokenization, the induced distribution <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math> is nothing but the text distribution induced by the stringification of tokens <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Particularly, if <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math> is associated with the true text distribution <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})=\mathbb{P}(a_{1:N}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}})=p_{\mathcal{V}}([a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}})=p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})=\mathbb{P}(a_{1:N}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}})=p_{\mathcal{V}}([a_{1:N}]_{\mathcal{V}})=p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">by <a href="#S2.E2" title="In Language model over tokens. ‣ 2.2 Formulation and Properties of Language Models ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Thus our definition of vocabulary reduction involves the previous byte-level reduction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vieira et al., 2025</a>)</cite> as its special case with <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}=\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}=\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the vocabulary reduction <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lossless</span>.
To see this, we consider the induced text distribution <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the text distribution obtained as the vocabulary reduction of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by another nested tokenization <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By iteratively applying <a href="#S3.E11" title="In Vocabulary reduction. ‣ 3.1 Formulation of Vocabulary Reduction ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y_{1:K}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})}[\mathds{1}\{a_{1:N}=[y_{1:K}]_{\mathcal{A}}\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y_{1:K}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})}[\mathds{1}\{a_{1:N}=[y_{1:K}]_{\mathcal{A}}\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})}[\mathds{1}\{a_{1:N}=[[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}]_{\mathcal{A}}\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})}[\mathds{1}\{a_{1:N}=[[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}]_{\mathcal{A}}\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})}[\mathds{1}\{a_{1:N}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:T}\sim p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})}[\mathds{1}\{a_{1:N}=[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{A}}\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By combining these equalities, we have proved the lossless property of vocabulary reduction:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{text}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{text}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the true text distribution underlying the language model <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let us denote the text distribution associated with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})=p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})=p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>text</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})=p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{A}}(a_{1:N})=p_{\mathrm{text}}(a_{1:N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Computation of the Next-Token Distribution</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At first glance, based on the above formulation, the computation of vocabulary reduction appears to be simple and easy at the level of probabilities over sentences, i.e., over <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
But in reality, the probabilities over sentences are computationally infeasible in the real world.
Instead, we have to compute the corresponding next-token distribution <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> using the original next-token distribution <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}\mid x_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}\mid x_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the next-token distribution <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})=\frac{p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k+1}*)}{p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)}=\frac{p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k+1}*)}{\sum_{y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k+1}*)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})=\frac{p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k+1}*)}{p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)}=\frac{p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k+1}*)}{\sum_{y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k+1}*)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">by its definition, the problem is how to compute the marginal distributions <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)</annotation></semantics></math>.
To answer this problem, we introduce the <span id="S3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">relative covering</span> <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math>, generalizing the minimal covering for <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vieira et al. (2025)</a></cite>, as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}):=\{x_{1:t}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}\mid x_{1:t}\text{ is valid and satisfies }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> is valid and satisfies</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}):=\{x_{1:t}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}\mid x_{1:t}\text{ is valid and satisfies }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E15.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">and</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle y_{1:k}\not\prec[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊀</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{1:k}\not\prec[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be as above. For any tokens <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)=\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)=\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is a generalization of Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1 ( ( ) ). ‣ Valid tokens and minimal covering. ‣ 2.2 Formulation and Properties of Language Models ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. See the proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proofs for ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The next problem is: how to efficiently compute the right hand side of <a href="#S3.E16" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>.
To answer this, we introduce the following subsets of the relative covering <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle C^{\mathrm{eq}}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}):=\{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\mid[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mi>eq</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C^{\mathrm{eq}}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}):=\{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\mid[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle C^{(l)}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}):=C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\cap\mathcal{V}^{l}=\{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\mid t=l\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C^{(l)}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}):=C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\cap\mathcal{V}^{l}=\{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\mid t=l\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then the summands in <a href="#S3.E16" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> can be decomposed into the following two cases.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies either</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">or (ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}\in C^{\mathrm{eq}}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mi>eq</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}\in C^{\mathrm{eq}}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\in C^{(l=1)}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\in C^{(l=1)}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">See the proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Appendix A Proofs for ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, for the case (ii), we remark that the valid tokens <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}\in C^{\mathrm{eq}}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mi>eq</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}\in C^{\mathrm{eq}}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math> can be uniquely determined as <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any valid<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Here we consider the validity with respect to <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> tokens <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Indeed, if <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}=[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}=[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and then <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}=[[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}=[[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the validity of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Conversely, if <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t-1}=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t-1}=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}=y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with the valid tokens <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=[[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}]=y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=[[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}]=y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> by its validity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By combining the above lemmas, we obtain the recursive formula to compute the desired probabilities:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any tokens <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that is valid with respect to the nested tokenization <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})\\
\text{\rm s.t.}\ y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)+\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{t}\in C^{(1)}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k}),\\
\text{with }x_{1:t-1}:=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≺</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">with </mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})\\
\text{\rm s.t.}\ y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)+\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{t}\in C^{(1)}_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k}),\\
\text{with }x_{1:t-1}:=[[y_{1:k-1}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the left-hand side is expanded as the sum of probabilities <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(x_{1:t}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{1:t}*)</annotation></semantics></math> over the relative cover <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we know that each summand <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies either (i) or (ii) in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, which leads to the decomposition shown in the right-hand side.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">An illustrative example.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, here we assume that <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of a set of bytes.
Let <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{-}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{-}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a token.
We suppose that the corresponding tokenizations are given by the greedy forward-matching tokenization, which maps each input bits <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{1}\cdots b_{N}\in\{0,1\}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\cdots b_{N}\in\{0,1\}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> to the longest matching tokens in the vocabulary, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, greedily from left to right.
Then we consider a language model <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> given by:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.5&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.6&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.5</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.6</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.5&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.6&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the tokens <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> are invalid since <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">001</annotation></semantics></math> is tokenized as <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle 001\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 001\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> in the greedy forward-matching tokenization, and thus the probability <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To compute <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we first calculate the relative covers:</p>
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 1\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 1\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then we can compute the marginal probabilities <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.8\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.8</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.8\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Now suppose that <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled.
To derive the next-token probability <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to consider the following relative covers:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 001\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 001\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Then the marginal probabilities <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)=\begin{cases}0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.2\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)=\begin{cases}0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.2\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Finally, we obtain the next-token distribution by normalizing the above marginal probabilities:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.25&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.375</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.375</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.25</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.25&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">From these results, we can easily check<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              The details are given in <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B An Example of Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> in Appendix.</span></span></span> that the probability of the output text starts from "000" is <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> in both models <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which demonstrates the lossless property shown in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Vocabulary reduction. ‣ 3.1 Formulation of Vocabulary Reduction ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Algorithm</h3>

<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Naive implementation.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the theoretical results in previous sections, we can derive an algorithm (<a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) to recursively compute and sample from next-token distributions <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, given only access to some autoregressive language model with the vocabulary <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., next-token distributions <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Due to its recursive nature, we can suppose that sub-tokens <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> have been sampled in previous iterations by this algorithm, and its intermediate outcomes are properly cached.
Under the circumstances, <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> computes the next-token distribution <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> and sample a next token <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> from it.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we explain how <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> produces the desired next-token distribution.
First of all, the given previous output <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> is re-tokenized in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}:=[[y_{1:k}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}:=[[y_{1:k}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then the next-token distribution <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}\mid x_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}\mid x_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by the given autoregressive language model (lines 1-2).
Note that here is the only part that requires access to the given language model in <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and the results are cached in the global memory <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> so that they can be reused in future iterations.
Then, in lines 3-17, the marginal probability <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}y_{k+1}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}y_{k+1}*)</annotation></semantics></math> is computed for each <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> by following <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.
More precisely, lines 7-11 implement the first term in <a href="#S3.E19" title="In Theorem 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, and lines 12-15 implement the second term.
Finally, in line 18, the sum is normalized over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the desired next-token distribution according to <a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Efficient implementation.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> has naively implemented the vocabulary reduction based on <a href="#S3.E16" title="In Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>.
Although the implementation is straightforward from the theoretical perspective,
it is computationally infeasible especially due to the two nested loops, lines 7-11 and lines 12-15.
Here we discuss how to deform <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> into a more efficient one, <a href="#alg2" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First of all, we consider the first nested loop (lines 7-11 in <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), which requires <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}|\times|C_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}|\times|C_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})|</annotation></semantics></math> iterations.
This part can be separated from the outer loop over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, because the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the condition in the line 8 is uniquely determined as the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th sub-token of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x^{\prime}_{1:t^{\prime}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x^{\prime}_{1:t^{\prime}}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus we can deform the lines 7-11 in <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> into the <span id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007091;">lines 7-11</span> in <a href="#alg2" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, which only requires <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|C_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})|</annotation></semantics></math> iterations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then we consider the second nested loop (lines 12-15 in <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), which requires <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}|\times|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}|\times|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> iterations.
This part can also be separated from the outer loop, because the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the condition in the line 13 is uniquely determined as the first sub-token of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x_{t+1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{t+1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the nested loop can be deformed into a single loop over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, we observe that the token <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with a low probability can be ignored as it will not contribute to the final summation.
Therefore we can restrict the single loop over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> to the one over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the top-<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> tokens with high probabilities.
Based on these observations, we can deform the lines 12-15 in <a href="#alg1" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> into the <span id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;">lines 12-16</span> in <a href="#alg2" title="In Efficient implementation. ‣ 3.3 Algorithm ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, which only requires <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> iterations.
Here <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary hyperparameter and we will set it to be a small number <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=300</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.fig1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:384.6pt;height:531.9pt;vertical-align:-525.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-33.9pt,46.9pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.fig1.1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:214.6pt;">
              
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Lossless Vocabulary Reduction (LVR).</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                      
                      
                    <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inputs:</span> Previously sampled tokens <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>sub</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                      
                      
                         a global cache <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> for computed probabilities,

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                      
                      
                         a global cache <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> for relative minimal covers.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                      
                      
                    <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outputs:</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}\mid y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                      
                      
                    
