<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs for <a href="#S3" title="3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be as in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Computation of the Next-Token Distribution ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. For any tokens <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)=\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)=\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here we introduce the following notation:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}^{(t)}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}^{(t)}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\cap\mathcal{V}^{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})\cap\mathcal{V}^{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have the following decomposition for the relative covering set:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})=\bigsqcup_{t\in\mathbb{N}}C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}^{(t)}(y_{1:k})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})=\bigsqcup_{t\in\mathbb{N}}C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}^{(t)}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using these notation, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k}*)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y_{1:K}\in y_{1:k}*}p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y_{1:K}\in y_{1:k}*}p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y_{1:K}\in y_{1:k}*}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:K}\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y_{1:K}\in y_{1:k}*}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:K}\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1:T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{T}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*,\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}-1]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\not\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*},\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*,\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}-1]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\not\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:t}\in\mathcal{V}^{t},\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*,\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}-1]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\not\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}\sum_{x_{t+1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{1:t}\in\mathcal{V}^{t},\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k}*,\\
[x_{1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\cdots[x_{t}-1]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\not\in y_{1:k}*\end{subarray}}\sum_{x_{t+1:T}\in\mathcal{V}^{*}}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}^{(t)}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}^{(t)}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})}p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1:t}*)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the notation in <a href="#S3" title="3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>,
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies either</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k}\prec[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">or (ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is valid and satisfies </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}\prec[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}\prec[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First of all, we note that <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:k^{\prime}}=[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:k^{\prime}}=[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math> by the assumption <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the last token <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expanded as <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{k^{\prime}+1:k}\cdots\in y_{k^{\prime}+1:k}*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">∈</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{k^{\prime}+1:k}\cdots\in y_{k^{\prime}+1:k}*</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the case of <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}=k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}=k-1</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}\prec[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}\prec[x_{t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and thus corresponds to the case (ii).
On the other hand, if <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}&lt;k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}&lt;k-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:t}\in C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k-1}*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1:t}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}\in y_{1:k-1}*</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k^{\prime}}\not\in y_{1:k-1}*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1:t-1}]_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}=y_{1:k^{\prime}}\not\in y_{1:k-1}*</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to the case (i).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>An Example of Lossless Vocabulary Reduction</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we assume that <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of a set of bytes.
Let <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}:=\{\langle 0\rangle,\langle 1\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{-}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{-}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a token.
We suppose that the corresponding tokenizations are given by the greedy forward-matching tokenization, which maps each input bits <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{1}\cdots b_{N}\in\{0,1\}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\cdots b_{N}\in\{0,1\}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> to the longest matching tokens in the vocabulary, <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, from left to right.
Then we consider a language model <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> given by:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.5&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.6&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.5</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.6</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.5&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{0}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.6&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }x_{1}=\langle 001\rangle,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the tokens <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> are invalid since <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">001</annotation></semantics></math> is tokenized as <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle 001\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 001\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> in the greedy forward-matching tokenization, and thus the probability <math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{1}=\langle 1\rangle\mid x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To compute <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we first calculate the relative covers:</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 1\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 1\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle,\langle 001\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then we can compute the marginal probabilities <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.8\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.8</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{0}*)=\begin{cases}0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.1\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.8\ \ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Now suppose that <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled.
To derive the next-token probability <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to consider the following relative covers:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 001\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\},\ C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle)=\{\langle 001\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{V},\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle)=\{\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle,\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Then the marginal probabilities <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)=\begin{cases}0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.2\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle y_{1}*)=\begin{cases}0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.3\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 1\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.2\ (=p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle*))&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Finally, we obtain the next-token distribution by normalizing the above marginal probabilities:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.25&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.375</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.375</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.25</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{1}\mid y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle)=\begin{cases}0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle,\\
0.375&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle,\\
0.25&amp;\text{if }y_{1}=\langle 00\rangle,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now we compare the corresponding text distributions for <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Especially, we calculate the probability that the output text starts with "000".
For the case of <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, such a probability is nothing but the probability of <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, since the text "<math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="000\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>000</mn><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">000\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>" can be tokenized as either <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>001</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 001\rangle\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>, by the greedy forward-matching tokenization.
On the other hand, for the case of <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the text "<math id="A2.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="000\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>000</mn><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">000\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>" can be tokenized as either <math id="A2.p3.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p3.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus the corresponding probability is given by <math id="A2.p3.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle*)=0.3+0.2=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 0\rangle*)+p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(\langle 00\rangle\langle 00\rangle*)=0.3+0.2=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the two distributions <math id="A2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> are equally plausible to output the text starting with "000".</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Also, here we can observe the following fact: even if two token-distributions are equivalent at the level of their byte-level distributions, <span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the texts obtained by greedy decoding may be different from each other in general</span>.
Indeed, on the one hand, the greedy decoding for the original distribution <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> generates the first token <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=\langle 00\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and the second token <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=\langle 0\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=\langle 0\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> according to equation (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Appendix B An Example of Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>).
On the other hand, the greedy decoding for the reduced distribution <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}\to\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math> may generate<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          This behavior is dependent on the implementation of greedy decoding sicne there are two tokens (<math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}=\langle 0\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>) achieving the maximal conditional probability.</span></span></span> <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>00</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}=\langle 00\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}=\langle 1\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> according to equation (<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Appendix B An Example of Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Appendix B An Example of Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), resulting in a different text <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">001</annotation></semantics></math> from the former one <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">000</annotation></semantics></math>, even though both distributions have the same text distribution by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Vocabulary reduction. ‣ 3.1 Formulation of Vocabulary Reduction ‣ 3 Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Setups</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen 2.5</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: A family of large language models developed by Qwen Team, ranging from 0.5B to 72B parameters. The tokenizer is implemented by the byte-level BPE with the vocabulary consisting of 151,665 tokens.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OLMo 2</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">OLMo et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: A family of large language models developed by Allen Institute for AI, ranging from 1B to 32B parameters. The tokenizer is implemented by the byte-level BPE with the vocabulary consisting of 100,278 tokens.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama 3.2</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meta, 2024</a>)</cite>: A family of large language models developed by Meta AI, ranging from 1B to 90B parameters. The tokenizer is implemented by the byte-level BPE with the vocabulary consisting of 128,256 tokens.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Falcon 3</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Falcon-LLM, 2024</a>)</cite>: A family of large language models developed by Technology Innovation Institute (TII), ranging from 1B to 10B parameters. The tokenizer is implemented by the byte-level BPE with the vocabulary consisting of 131,072 tokens.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used the following datasets for evaluating language models through the lm-evaluation-harness library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> with default options.</p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GSM8K</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>: A dataset consisting of grade-school math questions. Each question has an example of chain-of-thought argument followed by an open-ended answer. For each question, 5 pairs of a question and its answer are provided for language models by default. We reported the percentage of strictly-extracted correct answers.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MATH</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021b</a>)</cite>: A dataset of mathematical problem-solving tasks in 7 categories that require numerical and logical reasoning skills. Each question has an example of chain-of-thought argument followed by an open-ended answer. For each question, 4 pairs of a question and its answer are provided for language models, following the setting by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lewkowycz et al. (2022)</a></cite>. We reported the percentage of correct answers after which processed symbolically, with randomly sampled 100 questions from each category.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ACPBench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kokel et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: A dataset of tasks in 7 categories, evaluating the reasoning ability about action, change, and planning, with multiple answer choices. Each question has an example of chain-of-thought argument followed by the correct answer. For each question, 2 pairs of a question and its answer are provided for language models by default. We reported the percentage of correct answers for the questions with multiple choices, with randomly sampled 100 questions from each category.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMLU-Pro</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: A dataset of question-answering tasks in 14 categories, enhancing MMLU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021a</a>)</cite> by more challenging questions that require reasoning skills with multiple answer choices. Each question has an example of chain-of-thought argument followed by the correct answer. For each question, 5 pairs of a question and its answer are provided for language models by default. We reported the percentage of correct answers, with randomly sampled 100 questions from each category.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decoding method.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employed the greedy decoding for sampling tokens, i.e., iteratively sampling tokens with the highest probability, for both simpliticty and reproducibility. It is noteworthy that, even if two token distributions have the same text distribution, the resulting texts by greedy decoding for these models may be different from each other, as discussed in <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B An Example of Lossless Vocabulary Reduction ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Baselines</h3>

<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines for vocabulary reduction.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Naive Restriction</span>: Naive restriction is the most straightforward method for vocabulary reduction, but with no theoretical guarantee for accuracy. Let <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be a next-token distribution over <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a subset of <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. The naive restriction <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}|y_{1}\cdots y_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}}(y_{k+1}|y_{1}\cdots y_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as follows: Given previously sampled tokens <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1}\cdots y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}\cdots y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first retokenize it in <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1}\cdots x_{t}:=[[y_{1}\cdots y_{k}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\cdots x_{t}:=[[y_{1}\cdots y_{k}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we compute the next-token distribution <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, forcibly replace <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> by zero for all <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}\not\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}\not\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and renormalize it. Finally, we sample a next token <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}=x_{t+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}=x_{t+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the renormalized distribution.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Byte-Level Reduction</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: Since our lossless vocabulary reduction (LVR) can be seen as a generalization of the byte-level reduction proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al. (2025)</a></cite>, LVR with 1-byte tokens is actually equivalent to the byte-level reduction.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines for ensemble with different vocabularies.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ensemble over Union Vocabulary</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: Given language models <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> with different vocabularies <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can simply extend each next-token distribution <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{V}_{i}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{V}_{i}}(x_{t+1}|x_{1}\cdots x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> to the one over the union vocabulary <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\cup}:=\bigcup_{i}\mathcal{V}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∪</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\cup}:=\bigcup_{i}\mathcal{V}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by putting zero probabilities for <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\cup}\setminus\mathcal{V}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∪</mo></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}\in\mathcal{V}_{\cup}\setminus\mathcal{V}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
More specifically, to extend next-token distributions of the <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th model, given previous samples <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1}\cdots y_{k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\cup}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}\cdots y_{k}\in\mathcal{V}_{\cup}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first take the retokenization <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1}\cdots x_{t}:=[[y_{1}\cdots y_{k}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\cdots x_{t}:=[[y_{1}\cdots y_{k}]_{\mathcal{A}}]_{\mathcal{V}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and then compute the next-token distribution of the <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th model, following the procedure in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ensemble with Naive Restriction over MCV</span>: We just apply the naive restriction with <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}:=\mathcal{V}_{\cap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∩</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sub}}:=\mathcal{V}_{\cap}</annotation></semantics></math> (as defined in <a href="#S4" title="4 Application: Ensemble via Maximal Common Vocabulary ‣ Lossless Vocabulary Reduction for Auto-Regressive Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) to each language model, and then compute their ensemble distribution.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

